thon as the control plane","short":"State","main":"A list of five numbers, a state-reason pair.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["info","state","Constants","Reasons"],"captions":["info(): state, max memory KiB, memory KiB, vCPUs, cpuTime in ns","state(): a pair [state, reason]","VIR_DOMAIN_RUNNING = 1, PAUSED = 3, SHUTOFF = 5, CRASHED = 6","Reasons are numbered separately for each state"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["st, maxkib, kib, ncpu, cpu_ns = dom.info()","state, reason = dom.state()","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_RUNNING   # 1","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_PAUSED    # 3","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_SHUTOFF   # 5","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_CRASHED   # 6","# reason 1: booted (running), user (paused)"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["st, maxkib, kib, ncpu, cpu_ns = dom.info()","state, reason = dom.state()","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_RUNNING   # 1","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_PAUSED    # 3","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_SHUTOFF   # 5","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_CRASHED   # 6","# reason 1: booted (running), user (paused)"],"hl":[1],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["st, maxkib, kib, ncpu, cpu_ns = dom.info()","state, reason = dom.state()","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_RUNNING   # 1","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_PAUSED    # 3","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_SHUTOFF   # 5","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_CRASHED   # 6","# reason 1: booted (running), user (paused)"],"hl":[2,3,4,5],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["st, maxkib, kib, ncpu, cpu_ns = dom.info()","state, reason = dom.state()","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_RUNNING   # 1","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_PAUSED    # 3","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_SHUTOFF   # 5","libvirt.VIR_DOMAIN_CRASHED   # 6","# reason 1: booted (running), user (paused)"],"hl":[6],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[11.9,17.8,29.1]}]},{"title":"The life cycle","sub":"Chapter 25 · Python as the control plane","short":"Cycle","main":"define, create, shutdown with a deadline, then destroy.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["define","shutdown","destroy","undefine"],"captions":["defineXML makes a domain persistent, create starts it","shutdown only asks the guest and returns at once; the guest may refuse","destroy pulls the power cord; the GRACEFUL flag leaves only SIGTERM","undefine removes the definition; createXML starts a transient domain"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["dom = conn.defineXML(xml)    # persistent","dom.create()                 # start","dom.shutdown()               # ask the guest","# poll dom.state() until the deadline","dom.destroy()                # power cord","dom.destroyFlags(1)  # GRACEFUL: SIGTERM only","dom.undefine()               # drop definition"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["dom = conn.defineXML(xml)    # persistent","dom.create()                 # start","dom.shutdown()               # ask the guest","# poll dom.state() until the deadline","dom.destroy()                # power cord","dom.destroyFlags(1)  # GRACEFUL: SIGTERM only","dom.undefine()               # drop definition"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["dom = conn.defineXML(xml)    # persistent","dom.create()                 # start","dom.shutdown()               # ask the guest","# poll dom.state() until the deadline","dom.destroy()                # power cord","dom.destroyFlags(1)  # GRACEFUL: SIGTERM only","dom.undefine()               # drop definition"],"hl":[4,5],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["dom = conn.defineXML(xml)    # persistent","dom.create()                 # start","dom.shutdown()               # ask the guest","# poll dom.state() until the deadline","dom.destroy()                # power cord","dom.destroyFlags(1)  # GRACEFUL: SIGTERM only","dom.undefine()               # drop definition"],"hl":[6],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[8.0,18.7,28.8]}]},{"title":"Errors by code","sub":"Chapter 25 · Python as the control plane","short":"Errors","main":"The code, not the text, and a code-to-action table.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Code","Already done","Retry","Fail"],"captions":["get_error_code() instead of comparing the message text","42 NO_DOMAIN and 55 OPERATION_INVALID often mean the work is already done","9 OPERATION_FAILED and 68 OPERATION_TIMEOUT: retry, 5 NO_CONNECT: reconnect","Anything else: log it and fail loudly"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["try:","    dom = conn.lookupByName(name)","except libvirt.libvirtError as e:","    code = e.get_error_code()","    if code == libvirt.VIR_ERR_NO_DOMAIN:  # 42","        return None","    raise"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["try:","    dom = conn.lookupByName(name)","except libvirt.libvirtError as e:","    code = e.get_error_code()","    if code == libvirt.VIR_ERR_NO_DOMAIN:  # 42","        return None","    raise"],"hl":[4,5],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["try:","    dom = conn.lookupByName(name)","except libvirt.libvirtError as e:","    code = e.get_error_code()","    if code == libvirt.VIR_ERR_NO_DOMAIN:  # 42","        return None","    raise"],"hl":[4],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["try:","    dom = conn.lookupByName(name)","except libvirt.libvirtError as e:","    code = e.get_error_code()","    if code == libvirt.VIR_ERR_NO_DOMAIN:  # 42","        return None","    raise"],"hl":[6],"lang":"python","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[8.8,20.7,33.0]}]},{"title":"Snapshots","sub":"Chapter 25 · Python as the control plane","short":"Snapshots","main":"A tree of snapshots: 